- op: discuss  # 9aeb
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:09Z'  # 9aeb
  by: agent  # 9aeb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9aeb
  clock: 4  # 9aeb
  nonce: 9aeb  # 9aeb
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). PARTLY STALE (sub-item 1 fixed); sub-item 3 DISPUTED. Title updated to the four remaining rows.\n1. FIXED: erlang inet.gethostname is host_info_read (erlang.yaml:322-330), moved in 4f463b6722 (PR #839, WI-dozul's sort).\n2. STILL PRESENT: objc removeObserver: and removeObserver:name:object: are ipc_recv (objc.yaml:297-302).\n3. STILL PRESENT, PREMISE DISPUTED: python os.wait* are ipc_recv; os.waitpid reaches subprocess.run as a confirmed untrusted_input flow. But WI-lanos (todo_hard, filed after this item, sequenced behind WI-dozul) frames the exit status as \"eight bits the child chose\", a transfer under the WI-dozul rule, and shipped rows cite os.wait as precedent (rust Child.wait*, rust.yaml:469-480; INV-lozat notes in go/rust/python). This item's \"not data another process sent\" contradicts that. Decide it on WI-lanos (fold surfaced, not performed).\n4. STILL PRESENT: sqlite3 Connection.backup is db_read (python.yaml:516-518); reachable only with a typed receiver (annotation or sqlite3.Connection(...)), not via connect()'s return value. Direction is half right: backup reads the source db, writes the target, returns None. ADR-0049 Ruling 1 rules out the source, but a db_write sink's only argument would be a connection handle. The module_completeness note (python.yaml:1937, \"backup all rowed\") must change with it.\n5. STILL PRESENT: ets.info and mnesia.table_info are db_read (erlang.yaml:214,218); both mint untrusted_input reaching os:cmd (structural).\n- The discussion's \"sixth\" (ets:foldl) is not a catalogue change: ADR-0049 Ruling 4 records ets:foldl as a transfer, and its db_read row is correct.\n- Siblings not chased: objc addObserver* (route-registration shape, deferred under ADR-0049); dets.traverse still db_read though ADR-0049 calls it callback-delivered."  # 9aeb
