  clock: 6  # cd88
  nonce: cd88  # cd88
  message: "ROW 3 ONLY (python os.wait / wait3 / wait4 / waitid / waitpid), 2026-10-03, branch jgstern-agent/fix/lanos commit de6aacfe6c. Rows 2, 4 and 5 are another agent's (~/hg_wt/ragaz); I touched none of them.\n\nOUTCOME: row 3's premise is REJECTED, the rows stay ipc_recv. Decided by WI-lanos-busoj-lativ-minud-buton-vuviv-jihit-bumip (same branch, first commit), which reconciled the exit status under WI-dozul's owner ruling: the status is the value the child passed to exit(), a far-side CHOICE from a constrained set, which is a transfer under ADR-0049 ruling 1. This row's \"a status integer the kernel computed is not data another process sent\" is the reading WI-lanos rejected; host_info_read would describe THIS host, and no row would re-open the one-value-two-verdicts split, since subprocess.call / os.system / subprocess.run / Popen.wait now mint on the same value.\n\nCHANGE: note-only on the os.wait row in python.yaml, recording the decision at the row. No boundary, label or row-set change. Behaviour identical before and after: os.waitpid / os.wait fixtures through the production CLI read violated, ipc_recv, choice_shaped_source in both arms. No reachability fixture is owed for a row that does not move; the existing one (os.waitpid reaching subprocess.Popen) is pinned in tests/test_exit_status_is_one_verdict.py."  # cd88
- op: discuss  # efd6
